From 98f48610559a13808a330f5c3e117a5f109dbedd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cruz <jelon@tbu.net>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 17:44:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 011/206] feat(shorebird): field table link info -- content now
 exactly matches theirs

All 622 entries, max_field_id, and every (id, name, hash) triple are identical to
Shorebird's output; the multiset compares equal and sorting both sides makes them
match element for element. Output size is also exactly 47426 bytes.

Two encoding details were wrong before and are now recovered from their data:

  * kind_bits is masked. Bits 16 (NoSanitizeThreadBit) and 17
    (HasDeeplyImmutableTypeBit) never appear in their output -- we had 5 entries
    with bit 17 and 1 with bit 16 -- and masking exactly those two reconciles all
    11 previously differing entries. They describe the thread/memory model rather
    than field identity, so excluding them keeps the link info stable.
    NB: this supersedes the earlier guess that Shorebird builds with
    deeply-immutable disabled. That was wrong -- EnsureDeeplyImmutable and
    CheckedStoreIntoShared both appear in their binary, and those stubs are not
    conditionally compiled. The earlier assembly-size difference was a build mode
    difference, not a missing feature.

  * Duplicates repeat " 1" instead of incrementing a counter. ClassID's 93 field
    names each occur twice, emitted as "ClassID.cidNull 3 1" (id 0) and
    "ClassID.cidNull 3 1 1" (id 94). All 529 three-segment entries carry a
    constant trailing 1, so the first is always present and each further
    occurrence appends another.

The remaining difference is ordering within equal field_ids. Their order is not
alphabetical and not by owner class id (checked: owner cids run 501, 521, 187,
442, ... for id 1), so it is heap iteration order -- a function of heap layout,
not of this algorithm. Aligning it requires the two VMs to allocate identically,
which is the same class of constraint as the snapshot version hash.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/runtime/vm/shorebird/link_info.cc b/runtime/vm/shorebird/link_info.cc
index a1d8c442efb..558d9420034 100644
--- a/runtime/vm/shorebird/link_info.cc
+++ b/runtime/vm/shorebird/link_info.cc
@@ -266,9 +266,21 @@ FieldTableLinkInfo* GetFieldTableLinkInfo(Thread* thread) {
 
     std::string hash = qualified;
     hash += ' ';
-    hash += std::to_string(field.kind_bits());
-    hash += ' ';
-    hash += std::to_string(occurrence);
+    // Shorebird masks out NoSanitizeThreadBit (16) and
+    // HasDeeplyImmutableTypeBit (17): they describe the thread/memory model, not
+    // field identity, so leaving them in would make the link info depend on
+    // properties irrelevant to matching. Verified against their output -- those
+    // two bits never appear in it, and masking them reconciles all 11
+    // previously differing entries.
+    constexpr uint32_t kUnstableKindBits = (1u << 16) | (1u << 17);
+    hash += std::to_string(field.kind_bits() & ~kUnstableKindBits);
+    // Duplicates are marked by REPEATING " 1", not by an incrementing counter:
+    // ClassID's 93 field names each appear twice, emitted as "... 3 1" and
+    // "... 3 1 1". The first " 1" is therefore always present, and each further
+    // occurrence appends another one.
+    for (intptr_t n = 0; n < occurrence; n++) {
+      hash += " 1";
+    }
 
     const intptr_t id = field.field_id();
     max_field_id = Utils::Maximum(max_field_id, id);
